season one of jupiter's legacy sets up  many plot threads for future episodes to  explore  in addition to the massive villain  reveal in the season finale  the show also established how hutch  would go to the ends of the earth to  save his father  there's also the question of whether  chloe would ultimately follow in her  parents footsteps  and become the superhero they want her  to embody sadly those questions will  remain up in the air as jupiter's legacy  comic book writer mark miller  announced netflix released the cast from  their contracts  dooming any hopes of a follow-up miller  posted in his original tweet that he  remained hopeful a second season could  materialize at some point  but even if that does happen it will not  be anytime soon  after all netflix has its hands full  with a slew of other projects adapted  from the middleworld brand of comics and  miller even revealed in the tweet that  he had begun working on a live-action  series  based on supercrooks while netflix  hasn't released numbers regarding how  many people watch the superhero series  it didn't do too well with critics  garnering only a 38  rating on the tomato meter it likely  didn't help with the series prospects  despite its average audience score of 72  percent  looking through the various comments  that are poured in from twitter it's  clear the show did a massive form of a  fanbase  and those supporters have let their  opinions known that the show deserves a  second chance  one twitter user noted that there were  still plenty of stories to be told  i'm disappointed that jupiter's legacy  is getting effectively cancelled  it's had a lot of potential from its  source materials that could have been  explored in later seasons  in a search for answers some fans think  it came down to one thing  wigs in apparent jest maybe jess several  users make comments like  jupiter's legacy wouldn't have flopped  if they just gave that dude a better wig  and another added wow jupiter's legacy  is already cancelled solely because the  wigs were so bad  so maybe not just at all within a fan  outcry perhaps netflix could reconsider  the future of jupiter's legacy  probably not but fret not there's more  from the miller verse coming soon the  announcement of a live-action super  crook series is intriguing for a couple  of reasons  for starters in the comic books super  crooks takes place in the same universe  as the events of jupiter's legacy  so theoretically characters and events  from the netflix series  could make their way onto this new show  that instead focuses on the villains  secondly the super crook show miller  mentioned in his tweet  will be a different series from the  anime series also in development  as miller explained note super crooks  will appear first as an anime series  from studio bones later this year  other projects in the pipeline include  american jesus and the magic order  however there haven't been any  announcements regarding release dates as  of this time  anyone wanting more stories explicitly  set in the jupiter's legacy universe  does have a bit of luck miller has  worked on a new comic book series  jupiter's legacy requiem the first book  from the 12 issue series drops on june  16th  and it focuses on chloe hutch and their  children  as they continue trying to make earth  peaceful for now  it's the closest thing fans can get to  some semblance of closure  on the short-lived netflix series  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  comic book shows are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss  a single one
 

